What If the Sun Vanished? — flat-vector explainer (1080×1920, 24 fps)
Everything on screen is drawn in code (main.js + kit.js, canvas 2D): Earth, the Sun, the Moon, the photons, the person, the
sunflower, the sea, the ice, the vent and its creatures, the type. No images, no stock footage, no generated media. Our own character designs, in the
Beyond Everything brand style. Facts: FACTS.md.

Type
  Nunito — the Nunito Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (fonts/OFL-Nunito.txt), from github.com/google/fonts.
Voice
  Microsoft Edge neural voice "Ryan" (en-GB-RyanNeural, +5%), via edge-tts
  (same voice as the earlier Beyond Everything films).
Score and sound effects
  Original, synthesized in music.py and mix.py (numpy/scipy). No samples.
